summary: Leap second insert once test
description: |
    This test signals the kernel to insert a leap second
    10 seconds of midnight GMT. This allows for stessing the
    kernel's leap-second behavior.
    The test then checks to make sure TIME_WAIT is present at the time of change.
    States:
        TIME_OK, synchronized, no leap second warning
        TIME_INS, synchronized, leap second insertion warning
        TIME_DEL, synchronized, leap second deletion warning
        TIME_OOP, leap second in progress
        TIME_WAIT, leap second has occurred
        TIME_ERROR, clock not synchronized
    Test Inputs:
        leap-a-day.c is source that is compiled and enables testing of this issue. 
    Expected results:
        + RESULT=PASS
        + rstrnt-report-result general/time/leap-second/ins_leap_sec_once PASS 0
    Results location:
        output.txt
contact: Qiao Zhao <qzhao@redhat.com>
id: a6186ed8-e869-41a8-89c3-b4a23cf048c7
test: bash -x ./runtest.sh
framework: shell
require:
  - gcc
  - make
  - type: file
    pattern:
        - /cki_lib
duration: 5m
tier: 1
extra-summary: general/time/leap-second/ins_leap_sec_once
extra-task: general/time/leap-second/ins_leap_sec_once
